/* English texts.

   Left — the string as written in the source: that is the key, and the app
   looks the text up by it. Right — what the person sees.

   Missing keys are not an error: the app falls back to the key itself, which
   is the Russian source string. So a partial translation degrades to Russian
   line by line rather than breaking anything.

   %@ — substituted text, %lld — integer, %lf — decimal. They must survive
   translation, or the substitution is lost.
*/

